{
  "_readme": [
    "THE SEEDED NAMES AS THEY STOOD BEFORE WAVE 5, and the identity each one is given.",
    "",
    "A FROZEN RECORD, like `retired_presets.json` and `legacy_themes.json` beside it. It exists for one",
    "moment: `ensure_template_seed_identity` back-fills `templates.seed_key` by NAME against this list,",
    "which is the ONE instant name-matching is correct — it runs before anything in wave 5 has renamed a",
    "row. Nothing may add a name here later; a name added after that instant would match a row somebody",
    "created themselves.",
    "",
    "WHY A NAME AND NOT THE BYTES. RG-142 measured the previous, byte-matching retirement at 0 of 21",
    "against a copy of a real database. Two independent rewrites defeat a byte comparison, either fatal",
    "alone: `TemplateGallery.upgradeLegacyToLayers` converts a region template to the layer model and",
    "SAVES it on mount, with layer ids that fold in `performance.now()`; and `style_json` returns through",
    "serde_json's BTreeMap in alphabetical key order, not the seed's hand-written order. A name survives",
    "both. Its closing sentence is this file's whole design: anything surviving the conversion needs an",
    "identity the conversion preserves, not a byte comparison.",
    "",
    "A COLLISION DECLINES. If two rows carry one of these names at back-fill time, neither is stamped:",
    "one of them is somebody's own template that happens to share a name, and there is no way to tell",
    "which. Declining leaves both rows exactly where they are, which is the safe direction to fail in.",
    "",
    "EVERY KEY HERE BEGINS `legacy.`, and that prefix IS the retired set. A row wave 5 still ships",
    "carries its own key (`scripture.dayspring`, `timer.monolith`); a row it stopped shipping carries a",
    "`legacy.` one. `was` records which of the four lists the name came from and is a note to a reader.",
    "",
    "The fifty-seven: five built-ins, twenty-five family members, seven shelf looks and the twenty-one",
    "already frozen in `retired_presets.json` — `Lower Third · Scripture` being on two of those lists is",
    "why it is fifty-seven and not fifty-eight."
  ],
